WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.126 --> 00:00:03.890
- I'm back with Billy Gardell!

00:00:03.890 --> 00:00:05.246
Give it up for him!

00:00:05.246 --> 00:00:07.550
(audience cheers)

00:00:07.550 --> 00:00:10.460
His show is called "Bob Hearts Abishola".

00:00:10.460 --> 00:00:13.540
You can watch it on
CBS and CBS All Access.

00:00:13.540 --> 00:00:16.040
Say it five times fast,
Abishola, Abishola, Abishola.

00:00:16.040 --> 00:00:17.750
I'm gonna nail it by the end of the show.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:20.610
My next guest was named the Los Angeles

00:00:20.610 --> 00:00:22.743
Unified School District in L.A County

00:00:22.743 --> 00:00:26.640
2020-2021 Teacher Of The Year.

00:00:26.640 --> 00:00:29.130
That's a title, y'all, she dominates.

00:00:29.130 --> 00:00:33.230
Please welcome Mrs.
Rhiannon Chavez, give it up!

00:00:33.230 --> 00:00:34.460
(audience cheers)

00:00:34.460 --> 00:00:35.900
Meet Billy, first of all.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:36.777
- Hi Billy.

00:00:36.777 --> 00:00:38.900
- Hi, it's a pleasure to meet you,

00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:40.280
and thank you for what you do.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.910
- Thank you, nice to meet you.

00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:43.167
- I mean, his teacher
is amazing, we love him.

00:00:43.167 --> 00:00:45.250
So what do you teach?

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.270
What's your like specialty?

00:00:46.270 --> 00:00:47.103
What do you do?

00:00:47.103 --> 00:00:50.290
- I teach fourth grade at
186th Street Elementary School

00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:51.570
in Gardena.
- Yes.

00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:53.191
- I am an ELD teacher, which means

00:00:53.191 --> 00:00:55.660
I teach English language learners.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:58.796
So I've had students from
Cameroon speak French,

00:00:58.796 --> 00:01:01.260
from Brazil speaking Portuguese,

00:01:01.260 --> 00:01:03.530
from Egypt speaking Arabic.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.950
So as you can imagine,
my classroom is filled

00:01:05.950 --> 00:01:09.989
with culture, language,
love, and lots of learning.

00:01:09.989 --> 00:01:11.517
- Wow.

00:01:11.517 --> 00:01:12.350
- But you know what?

00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:13.710
They come in with so much already,

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.920
especially with their language,

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:17.490
and talking with all the
kids on the playground,

00:01:17.490 --> 00:01:19.629
they pick up on a lot of language.

00:01:19.629 --> 00:01:22.200
- That's the ones you don't want, yes.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:24.760
- So why did you want to become a teacher?

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:27.873
I loved school and everything
about it when I was little,

00:01:27.873 --> 00:01:31.686
and I had great teachers, but
I never saw myself in them.

00:01:31.686 --> 00:01:34.130
Nobody looked like me.

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:37.652
So when I became a teacher's
assistant for a middle school,

00:01:37.652 --> 00:01:39.140
a lot of the young girls,

00:01:39.140 --> 00:01:41.670
they would look up to me and admire me.

00:01:41.670 --> 00:01:43.150
And they say, you're going to college?

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:45.110
You traveled where over the weekend?

00:01:45.110 --> 00:01:46.989
And so I really felt that I could inspire

00:01:46.989 --> 00:01:49.970
little girls that look
like me in my community.

00:01:49.970 --> 00:01:52.110
So I said, I'm gonna be a teacher.

00:01:52.110 --> 00:01:53.428
- Representation.
- Yeah, exactly.

00:01:53.428 --> 00:01:54.510
- It's very important.

00:01:54.510 --> 00:01:57.420
- Yes, so I'm doing what I love.

00:01:57.420 --> 00:01:58.960
And it's a passion in my heart.

00:01:58.960 --> 00:02:02.750
And I think with teaching,
it always is that passion.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:03.730
- You have to have passion.

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:05.480
I have watched my mom in
a classroom and I'm like,

00:02:05.480 --> 00:02:09.730
whoa the patience of
Job, that one. (laughs)

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:11.720
- Can't learn it in a
book, that's for sure.

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:12.850
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:12.850 --> 00:02:15.920
And you have to be so patient and calm.

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:18.460
- But sometimes they get
a little chatty, Kelly.

00:02:18.460 --> 00:02:21.338
- [Kelly] Oh, you know
what, we are the same human.

00:02:21.338 --> 00:02:25.238
- And in my toolbox, I
have the teacher look.

00:02:25.238 --> 00:02:28.600
Every teacher has the teacher look.

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:31.450
So that saves me a couple of
times during our Zoom sessions.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:33.920
- Yes, see, I grew up with
a teacher for a mother.

00:02:33.920 --> 00:02:36.400
So this was the same look was like

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:38.820
oh my God, I'm in so much trouble.

00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:40.860
Like it was the same
look, can you show us?

00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.643
I have to ask you,
what's your teacher look?

00:02:43.830 --> 00:02:44.820
Oh, God, see?

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:49.820
Oh, the slow blink, the slow
blink, that was amazing!

00:02:50.190 --> 00:02:51.023
- I'll wait.

00:02:51.023 --> 00:02:53.441
- I'll wait. (laughs)

00:02:53.441 --> 00:02:54.750
- There's the look.

00:02:54.750 --> 00:02:57.163
- Oh god, I love the
slow blink, I love it.

00:02:58.080 --> 00:03:00.695
We're basically sweating,
Billy and I, 'cause we,

00:03:00.695 --> 00:03:04.430
I don't know, I'm a part of this show,

00:03:04.430 --> 00:03:05.720
I don't know why I did this to myself.

00:03:05.720 --> 00:03:06.910
I have not seen these questions,

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:09.257
but apparently there is
a fourth grade pop quiz

00:03:09.257 --> 00:03:11.298
that you are gonna give me and Billy.

00:03:11.298 --> 00:03:12.150
- Oh, yes.

00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:15.560
- Okay, let's not judge, I
just wanna lead with that

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:17.127
because we all have our strengths,

00:03:17.127 --> 00:03:19.893
and we all have our weaknesses.

00:03:21.006 --> 00:03:24.065
- Can we just be a team,
instead of two people?

00:03:24.065 --> 00:03:26.080
- No, I'm gonna kill you!

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:28.620
- I need a lifeline.

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:31.910
- Okay, we'll each answer one at a time.

00:03:31.910 --> 00:03:35.350
And if we don't know
the answer or are wrong,

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:37.100
the other person can have a guess.

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:40.350
So if I get more correct the right side

00:03:40.350 --> 00:03:42.550
of the audience gets a prize.

00:03:42.550 --> 00:03:45.600
And if Billy gets more
correct, no pressure Billy,

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:47.749
but the left side will get a prize.

00:03:47.749 --> 00:03:51.960
I feel like I'm at the chalkboard
and I'm having to do math.

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.730
Oh, okay.

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:55.040
- Question number one.

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:57.130
- Okay, Billy, you can have the first one.

00:03:57.130 --> 00:04:01.580
- Billy, question number one,
category, social studies.

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:04.393
What are the three branches of government?

00:04:05.860 --> 00:04:08.963
- Legislative, Judicial,

00:04:10.068 --> 00:04:13.280
and I don't know what the word for it is.

00:04:13.280 --> 00:04:15.230
- It's legislative, it's judicial,

00:04:15.230 --> 00:04:18.050
and it is the president's, right?

00:04:18.050 --> 00:04:21.513
- The real term is executive.

00:04:21.513 --> 00:04:23.087
- Executive, whatever executive.

00:04:23.087 --> 00:04:25.793
But that's the part that
was the presidents, right?

00:04:26.709 --> 00:04:27.542
- Technically, yes.

00:04:27.542 --> 00:04:29.720
- I say technically it's okay.

00:04:31.930 --> 00:04:35.210
- Question number two,
category, language arts.

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:36.070
- [Kelly] Okay.

00:04:36.070 --> 00:04:39.255
- What punctuation goes
before a conjunction?

00:04:39.255 --> 00:04:41.316
- Before a conjunction?

00:04:41.316 --> 00:04:44.610
♪ Conjunction junction,
what's your function ♪

00:04:44.610 --> 00:04:46.180
Is it like, you mean the apos-

00:04:46.180 --> 00:04:47.470
Like when you do cannot, you make can't?

00:04:47.470 --> 00:04:49.590
Like a apostrophe, is that what you mean?

00:04:49.590 --> 00:04:53.200
- A comma, comma conjunction.

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.855
- Oh my God no, I thought it was,

00:04:54.855 --> 00:04:56.570
that's not even anywhere near right?

00:04:56.570 --> 00:04:58.780
Like can and not, and can't what is that?

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:01.600
- I think you're thinking
of a contraction.

00:05:01.600 --> 00:05:03.320
- A contraction!

00:05:03.320 --> 00:05:04.760
I'm thinking of a contraction.

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:06.280
You know what?

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:08.030
Oh, this is gonna be bad.

00:05:08.030 --> 00:05:10.140
- Thank God you can sing
and I can tell jokes.

00:05:10.140 --> 00:05:12.590
- I know man.

00:05:12.590 --> 00:05:14.700
- And I can correct your papers.

00:05:14.700 --> 00:05:17.560
Last question category is science.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:20.310
What is the smallest planet?

00:05:20.310 --> 00:05:22.788
- Wait, this is a trick, this is a trick.

00:05:22.788 --> 00:05:24.730
We're gonna go together on this one.

00:05:24.730 --> 00:05:26.520
'Cause Pluto used to
be the smallest plate.

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:27.789
But now it's like a dwarf planet.

00:05:27.789 --> 00:05:29.927
- Yeah, I don't know why we,

00:05:29.927 --> 00:05:34.540
I'm not sure why we cut
Pluto out of the club.

00:05:34.540 --> 00:05:36.390
It was a standard when I was growing up.

00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:37.223
I don't know what it did wrong.

00:05:37.223 --> 00:05:38.370
- Me too, brother.

00:05:38.370 --> 00:05:39.840
And then now it's like a dwarf,

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:40.910
and I don't know if they're counting it.

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:43.036
This could be a trick question.

00:05:43.036 --> 00:05:46.070
- Yeah, I would say if
we're counting Pluto in,

00:05:46.070 --> 00:05:49.380
it might be Pluto, but if
we're not counting Pluto in,

00:05:49.380 --> 00:05:52.593
I would say Mercury.
(bell dings)

00:05:53.625 --> 00:05:54.660
- Good job!

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.650
Wait, which one was right?

00:05:55.650 --> 00:05:56.980
Are you counting Pluto?

00:05:56.980 --> 00:05:58.364
- We don't count Pluto anymore.

00:05:58.364 --> 00:06:01.530
- This is my thing, can
we talk about new math?

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:03.320
'Cause here's my thing.

00:06:03.320 --> 00:06:07.500
Like all of a sudden
my niece and my nephew,

00:06:07.500 --> 00:06:08.620
'cause I got little toddlers,

00:06:08.620 --> 00:06:10.170
like, so they're not there yet.

00:06:11.164 --> 00:06:13.780
Like, there's some kind
of math, common core math,

00:06:13.780 --> 00:06:16.700
and it's like two plus
two could equal five.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:18.790
That's some BS.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:23.063
Okay, the winner is
Billy 'cause I'm a loser.

00:06:25.400 --> 00:06:27.220
I love that my whole life I thought

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:29.620
Conjunction Junction was just about,

00:06:29.620 --> 00:06:32.230
I don't know, it was a
contraction, it's fine.

00:06:32.230 --> 00:06:34.490
But because everyone in
our house seats today

00:06:34.490 --> 00:06:38.130
is a hardworking teacher,
you're definitely all winners.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:42.420
So we're gifting everyone
$100 credit to Gilt.

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:44.660
At Gilt you can get insider access

00:06:44.660 --> 00:06:47.170
to designer brands at unbelievable prices.

00:06:47.170 --> 00:06:49.000
They have great new sales every day

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:51.550
in apparel, accessories, home and beauty.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:52.853
Enjoy y'all.

00:06:54.600 --> 00:06:56.540
Thank you so much, Mrs. Chavez,

00:06:56.540 --> 00:06:58.240
for embarrassing me on television.

00:06:59.510 --> 00:07:00.624
- You're fine, you're fine.

00:07:00.624 --> 00:07:04.040
- And thank you so much for playing Billy.

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:04.930
I know you've got to run,

00:07:04.930 --> 00:07:07.200
so I'll see you later, man, all right?

00:07:07.200 --> 00:07:09.280
- Nice meeting you, and
have a great day you guys.

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:10.113
Thank you for having me.

00:07:10.113 --> 00:07:11.310
- You too, man, have a blessed one.

00:07:11.310 --> 00:07:13.870
All right, y'all can see
"Bob Heart's Abishola"

00:07:13.870 --> 00:07:15.953
